  "name": "Question 18",
  "problem": "Identify the sentence that is equivalent to the following: \"$x$ is rational, and $x$ is less than $2$ and it is rational.\"",
  "worked_solution": "Using the commutative law, we can replace the phrase \"$x$ is less than $2$ and it is rational\" with the phrase \"$x$ is rational and it is less than $2.$\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$x$ is rational, and $x$ is rational and it is less than $2.$\"\n\nThen, using the associative law, we can move the comma:\n\n\"$x$ is rational and $x$ is rational, and it is less than $2.$\"\n\nNow, we can simplify the phrase \"$x$ is rational and $x$ is rational\" to just \"$x$ is rational.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$x$ is rational, and it is less than $2.$\"\n\nFinally, we can write the sentence more concisely:\n\n\"$x$ is rational and less than $2.$\"",
